1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,130
Binary search is an ultra-fast algorithm to find a target in a sorted list by repeatedly halving the search space.

2
00:00:09,130 --> 00:00:17,469
We check the middle element. If our target is smaller, we discard the right half entirely.

3
00:00:17,469 --> 00:00:27,390
Calculate the mid index. If match found, return it. Otherwise adjust low or high boundary.

4
00:00:27,390 --> 00:00:35,609
In each step, half of the remaining elements disappear, yielding logarithmic O of log N speed.

5
00:00:35,609 --> 00:00:44,399
Binary search only works on sorted collections so that halving correctly determines which half contains the target.

